    "Category": "Dynamic Programming",
    "Front": "**Paint House**\nThere are a row of n houses, each can be painted red, blue, or green. No two adjacent houses can be painted the same color. Return the minimum cost to paint all houses.\n\nExample:\nInput: costs = [[17,2,17],[16,16,5],[14,3,19]]\nOutput: 10",
    "Back": "DP: dp[i][c] = min cost to paint up to house i with color c. For each house, pick min of the two other colors from previous house.\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def minCost(self, costs):\n        for i in range(1, len(costs)):\n            costs[i][0] += min(costs[i-1][1], costs[i-1][2])\n            costs[i][1] += min(costs[i-1][0], costs[i-1][2])\n            costs[i][2] += min(costs[i-1][0], costs[i-1][1])\n        return min(costs[-1])\n```"
  },
