    "Category": "Dynamic Programming",
    "Front": "**Dungeon Game**\nThe knight is trapped in a dungeon. He can only move right or down. Return the minimum initial health needed to reach the princess.\n\nExample:\nInput: dungeon = [[-2,-3,3],[-5,-10,1],[10,30,-5]]\nOutput: 7",
    "Back": "Work backwards from the bottom right. For each cell, compute the minimum health needed to survive, then add the cell’s value, making sure it never drops below 1.\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def calculateMinimumHP(self, dungeon):\n        m, n = len(dungeon), len(dungeon[0])\n        dp = [[float('inf')]*(n+1) for _ in range(m+1)]\n        dp[m][n-1] = dp[m-1][n] = 1\n        for i in range(m-1, -1, -1):\n            for j in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n                need = min(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j+1]) - dungeon[i][j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(1, need)\n        return dp[0][0]\n```"
  },
