    "Category": "Dynamic Programming",
    "Front": "**Cherry Pickup II**\nGiven a grid, two robots start at the first row and can move down/diagonally. Collect the maximum number of cherries. Return the max cherries both can collect.\n\nExample:\nInput: grid = [[3,1,1],[2,5,1],[1,5,5],[2,1,1]]\nOutput: 24",
    "Back": "Use DP with three dimensions: row, col1, col2. At each step, both robots move independently; maximize the total cherries collected.\n\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def cherryPickup(self, grid):\n        m, n = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n        from functools import lru_cache\n        @lru_cache(None)\n        def dp(r, c1, c2):\n            if c1 < 0 or c2 < 0 or c1 >= n or c2 >= n:\n                return 0\n            res = grid[r][c1] + (grid[r][c2] if c1 != c2 else 0)\n            if r < m-1:\n                res += max(dp(r+1, new_c1, new_c2)\n                           for new_c1 in [c1, c1+1, c1-1]\n                           for new_c2 in [c2, c2+1, c2-1])\n            return res\n        return dp(0, 0, n-1)\n```"
  },
